{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Functional SoV scalar product at zero twist — gl(3), L = 2, adjoint ⊗ adjoint\n\nSites: `[2,1,0] ⊗ [2,1,0]` (non-rectangular), inhomogeneities `θ1, θ2`, shift `h`, **no twist**.\n\nThe construction follows eqs. (12.38)–(12.42) of the SoV lecture notes (gl(3) case):\n\n$$\\mathcal O = 1 - \\frac{T_{1,1}}{\\nu_1}\\mathcal D^{-1} + \\frac{T_{2,1}}{\\nu_1\\nu_1^{[-2]}}\\mathcal D^{-2} - \\frac{T_{3,1}}{\\nu_1\\nu_1^{[-2]}\\nu_1^{[-4]}}\\mathcal D^{-3},\\qquad \\mathcal O^\\dagger = 1 - \\frac{T^{[2]}_{1,1}}{\\nu_3^{[2]}}\\mathcal D + \\frac{T^{[4]}_{2,1}}{\\nu_3^{[2]}\\nu_3^{[4]}}\\mathcal D^{2} - \\frac{T^{[6]}_{3,1}}{\\nu_3^{[2]}\\nu_3^{[4]}\\nu_3^{[6]}}\\mathcal D^{3},$$\n\n$$\\mathcal O\\,q_i^{[2]} = 0,\\qquad \\mathcal O^\\dagger q^j = 0,\\qquad 0 = \\oint \\frac{\\Gamma[\\nu_1^{[2]}]}{\\Gamma[\\nu_3^{[2]}]}\\, q^j_A\\,(\\mathcal O^A-\\mathcal O^B)\\,q_i^{B[2]} .$$\n\nTemplate: `SU4_SoV_Orthogonality_Untwisted_L2.wb` (gl(4), rectangular). Generators: GT construction ported verbatim from `SU4_L1.wb` (valid for any gl(N)). Transfer matrices are built **explicitly** from the Lax matrix on the 64-dim space, not from a closed form, since for non-rectangular sites nothing is known yet.\n\nConventions: `f^{[±2n]}(u) = f(u ± n h)`, `L_{ij}(u) = u δ_{ij} - h E_{ji}`, `T(u) = L^{(1)}(u-θ1) L^{(2)}(u-θ2)`, `ν_i(u) = (u-θ1-hλ_i)(u-θ2-hλ_i)` with `λ = {2,1,0}`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 0. gl(N) generators in the Gelfand-Tsetlin basis, ported verbatim from SU4_L1.wb (rank-independent). ---- *)\nClearAll[ps, dim, J0, Jp, Jm, JJ, v];\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #] & /@ (Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]))}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse@Sort@res, Reverse@Sort@Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]], l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]], l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]], l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep], l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\n(* single-site checks for the adjoint: dimension and the gl(3) commutation relations [E_ij, E_kl] = δ_jk E_il - δ_li E_kj *)\nWith[{r = {2, 1, 0}}, Grid[{{\"dim [2,1,0]\", dim[r]}, {\"gl(3) relations hold\", And @@ Flatten[Table[JJ[i, j, r] . JJ[k, l, r] - JJ[k, l, r] . JJ[i, j, r] == KroneckerDelta[j, k] JJ[i, l, r] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] JJ[k, j, r], {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}, {l, 3}]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"714828\" data-output-id=\"11\" data-out-n=\"8\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"1\" data-sub-start=\"9\" data-sub-end=\"9\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[8]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"38\" data-latex-b64=\"XGJlZ2lue2FycmF5fXt8Y3xjfH1caGxpbmVcdGV4dHtkaW0gWzIsMSwwXX0gJiA4XFxcaGxpbmVcdGV4dHtnbCgzKSByZWxhdGlvbnMgaG9sZH0gJiBcbWF0aHJte1RydWV9XFxcaGxpbmVcZW5ke2FycmF5fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.44em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dim [2,1,0]</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">gl(3) relations hold</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">8</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[8]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{dim [2,1,0]} & 8\\\\\\hline\\text{gl(3) relations hold} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "fea5de8e-2bd4-496d-a983-21655d8c4e6d"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Two-site chain and transfer matrices\n\n`T_{a,1}(u) = Σ_{|I|=a} qmin[I,I](u)` with the quantum minors `qmin[I,J](u) = Σ_σ sgn σ T_{I_σ1 J_1}(u) T_{I_σ2 J_2}(u-h) ⋯` (same ordering as `SU4_L1.wb`). All operators are exact 64×64 matrices, symbolic in `u, θ1, θ2, h`. Checks: commutativity, quantum determinant central, and the highest-weight eigenvalues of the diagonal `T_ii` (which fix `ν_i`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 1. Two-site monodromy and transfer matrices, adjoint x adjoint, zero twist. ---- *)\nClearAll[rep, d1, id1, E1, E2, Lax, Tm, qmin, tt, tco, Etot, u, θ1, θ2, h];\nrep = {2, 1, 0}; d1 = dim[rep]; id1 = IdentityMatrix[d1];\nE1[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[JJ[i, j, rep], id1];\nE2[i_, j_] := E2[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[id1, JJ[i, j, rep]];\nEtot[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] + E2[i, j];\n(* L_ij(u) = u δ_ij - h E_ji, one per site; T = L1(u-θ1) L2(u-θ2) in auxiliary space *)\nTm[i_, j_][x_] := Expand[Sum[((x - θ1) KroneckerDelta[i, k] IdentityMatrix[d1^2] - h E1[k, i]) . ((x - θ2) KroneckerDelta[k, j] IdentityMatrix[d1^2] - h E2[j, k]), {k, 3}]];\nqmin[II_List, KK_List][x_] := Expand[Sum[Signature[σ] (Dot @@ Table[Tm[II[[σ[[k]]]], KK[[k]]][x - (k - 1) h], {k, Length[II]}]), {σ, Permutations[Range[Length[II]]]}]];\n(* operator-valued polynomial coefficients of the three transfer matrices *)\nAbsoluteTiming[tt[1] = qmin[{#}, {#}][u] & /@ Range[3] // Total; tt[2] = Total[qmin[#, #][u] & /@ Subsets[Range[3], {2}]]; tt[3] = qmin[{1, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}][u];]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"714828\" data-output-id=\"12\" data-out-n=\"16\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"3\" data-sub-start=\"10\" data-sub-end=\"10\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[16]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"38\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezEuOTgxMDk0LFxtYXRocm17TnVsbH1ccmlnaHRcfQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">1.981094</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Null</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[16]= \\left\\{1.981094,\\mathrm{Null}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "e3a04379-8297-472d-8ca6-584014969465"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 1b. Checks: [T_a(u), T_b(v)] = 0 coefficientwise, T_3 = quantum determinant, gl(3) invariance at zero twist. ---- *)\nClearAll[ν, ν1, ν2, ν3, qdet];\nν[i_][x_] := (x - θ1 - h rep[[i]]) (x - θ2 - h rep[[i]]);\nν1[x_] := ν[1][x]; ν2[x_] := ν[2][x]; ν3[x_] := ν[3][x];\nqdet[x_] := ν1[x - 2 h] ν2[x - h] ν3[x];\ntco[a_, k_] := tco[a, k] = Coefficient[tt[a], u, k];\ncommChk = And @@ Flatten[Table[Expand[tco[a, k] . tco[b, l] - tco[b, l] . tco[a, k]] === ConstantArray[0, {64, 64}], {a, 2}, {b, a, 2}, {k, 0, 2 a}, {l, 0, 2 b}]];\nqdetChk = Expand[tt[3] - qdet[u] IdentityMatrix[64]] === ConstantArray[0, {64, 64}];\ninvChk = And @@ Flatten[Table[Expand[tco[a, k] . Etot[i, j] - Etot[i, j] . tco[a, k]] === ConstantArray[0, {64, 64}], {a, 2}, {k, 0, 2 a}, {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nGrid[{{\"[T_a(u), T_b(v)] = 0, a,b ∈ {1,2}\", commChk}, {\"T_3 = ν1[-4] ν2[-2] ν3\", qdetChk}, {\"[T_a, E_ij^tot] = 0 (zero twist)\", invChk}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"714828\" data-output-id=\"13\" data-out-n=\"25\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"4\" data-sub-start=\"9\" data-sub-end=\"9\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[25]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"38\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:3.64em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.09em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:3.6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">[T_a(u), T_b(v)] = 0, a,b </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"> {1,2}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">T_3 = </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.06366em;\">ν</span><span class=\"mord\">1[-4] </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.06366em;\">ν</span><span class=\"mord\">2[-2] </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.06366em;\">ν</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">[T_a, E_ij</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">tot] = 0 (zero twist)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:3.6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:3.6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[25]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{[T\\_a(u), T\\_b(v)] = 0, a,b $\\in$ \\{1,2\\}} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{T\\_3 = $\\nu$1[-4] $\\nu$2[-2] $\\nu$3} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{[T\\_a, E\\_ij\\^{}tot] = 0 (zero twist)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "56a344ca-7307-4574-aa6c-b0c1ca716507"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Highest-weight eigenstates\n\n`8 ⊗ 8 = 27 ⊕ 10 ⊕ 10̄ ⊕ 8 ⊕ 8 ⊕ 1`, highest weights `{4,2,0}, {3,3,0}, {4,1,1}, {3,2,1}×2, {2,2,2}`. At zero twist the transfer matrices commute with gl(3), so they act on each highest-weight space; only the `{3,2,1}` space is 2-dimensional, and there `T_2` splits the two octets. That is the sharp test: same weight, same Casimirs, `T_1` identical, only `T_2` differs.\n\nStructure of the eigenvalues (proved at operator level, symbolic `θ1, θ2, h`):\n- `T_1 = 3u^2 + b_1 u + t_1`, `b_1` fixed by `Σμ = 6`, so `ΔT_1 = Δt_1` (a constant);\n- `T_2 = 3u^4 + b_2 u^3 + (t_1 + c) u^2 + t_{21} u + t_{20}`, so `ΔT_2 = Δt_1 u^2 + Δt_{21} u + Δt_{20}`;\n- the octet splitting of `T_2` is a constant ∝ `h^3√(4h^2 + 5(θ1-θ2)^2)`.\n\nSo **three** independent differences `(Δt_1, Δt_{21}, Δt_{20})` enter. The numerical point `θ1 = 1/3, θ2 = -8/57, h = 1` has `θ1-θ2 = 9/19 ∉ ℤ` and makes the square root rational (`43/19`), so everything below is exact rational.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 2. Operator-level structure of T1, T2, then exact eigenvalues on every highest-weight state. ---- *)\nClearAll[prm, wtOf, hwBasis, hwStates, strChk, eigChk, a0, b0, c0];\nprm = {θ1 -> 1/3, θ2 -> -8/57, h -> 1};\n(* [u^2]T2 = [u^0]T1 + const, [u^4]T2 = 3, [u^3]T2 = const, as 64x64 operators (symbolic) *)\nstrChk = Module[{sol}, Table[sol = Solve[Thread[Flatten[tco[2, k]] == a0 Flatten[tco[1, 0]] + b0 Flatten[IdentityMatrix[64]]], {a0, b0}]; {k, If[sol === {}, \"not in span{[u^0]T1, 1}\", Simplify[{a0, b0} /. First[sol]]]}, {k, {4, 3, 2, 1, 0}}]];\nwtOf = Transpose[Table[Diagonal[Etot[i, i]], {i, 3}]];\nhwBasis[w_] := Module[{idx = Flatten@Position[wtOf, w]}, Transpose@Table[ReplacePart[ConstantArray[0, 64], Thread[idx -> nv]], {nv, NullSpace[Join[Etot[1, 2], Etot[2, 3]][[All, idx]]]}]];\n(* for each highest weight: restrict T1, T2 to the hw space, diagonalise jointly (exact at prm), one record per state *)\nhwStates = Flatten[Table[Module[{Bt = hwBasis[w], r, T1r, T2r, evs, ev, p},\n     r = First@Select[Subsets[Range[64], {Length[Bt[[1]]]}], Det[Bt[[#]]] =!= 0 &, 1];\n     T1r = Expand[Inverse[Bt[[r]]] . (tt[1] . Bt)[[r]] /. prm]; T2r = Expand[Inverse[Bt[[r]]] . (tt[2] . Bt)[[r]] /. prm];\n     evs = Eigenvectors[T2r /. u -> 0];\n     Table[ev = evs[[c]]; p = First@Flatten@Position[Unitize[ev], 1];\n      <|\"mu\" -> w, \"copy\" -> c, \"vec\" -> Bt . ev, \"T1\" -> Expand[(T1r . ev)[[p]]/ev[[p]]], \"T2\" -> Expand[(T2r . ev)[[p]]/ev[[p]]]|>, {c, Length[evs]}]],\n    {w, {{4, 2, 0}, {3, 3, 0}, {4, 1, 1}, {3, 2, 1}, {2, 2, 2}}}], 1];\n(* check: each record is a genuine eigenvector of the full 64x64 T1(u), T2(u) *)\neigChk = And @@ Flatten@Table[Expand[(tt[a] /. prm) . s[\"vec\"] - s[{\"T1\", \"T2\"}[[a]]] s[\"vec\"]] === ConstantArray[0, 64], {s, hwStates}, {a, 2}];\nColumn[{Grid[Prepend[strChk, {\"k\", \"[u^k]T2 = a [u^0]T1 + b : {a,b}\"}], Frame -> All],\n  Grid[{{\"all records are eigenvectors of T1(u), T2(u)\", eigChk}}, Frame -> All],\n  Grid[Prepend[{#[\"mu\"], #[\"copy\"], #[\"T1\"], #[\"T2\"]} & /@ hwStates, {\"mu\", \"copy\", \"T1(u)\", \"T2(u)\"}], Frame -> All]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
