   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Results (exact, `θ1 = 1/3, θ2 = -8/57, h = 1`)\n\n- **Chain (cells 3–5).** `[T_a(u), T_b(v)] = 0`; `T_3 = ν_1^{[-4]}ν_2^{[-2]}ν_3` is central; the `T_a` commute with total gl(3). Highest weights `{4,2,0}, {3,3,0}, {4,1,1}, {3,2,1}×2, {2,2,2}`; all six records are eigenvectors of the full 64×64 `T_1(u), T_2(u)`.\n- **Integrals of motion.** At operator level `[u^4]T_2 = 3`, `[u^3]T_2` = const, `[u^2]T_2 = [u^0]T_1` + const; `[u^1]T_2`, `[u^0]T_2` are independent. So three differences `(Δt_1, Δt_{21}, Δt_{20})` enter (vs two for rectangular gl(4)). `T_1` does not separate `10` from `10̄`, nor the two octets; `T_2` does.\n- **Q-functions (cell 9).** Three polynomial solutions each side, `deg q_i = (4 - μ_i) + (i-1)`, `deg q^j = μ_j + (3-j)`.\n- **Identity (cell 11).** `L_s[μ q^j_A O^A q_i^{B[2]}] = 0` for all 30 ordered cross pairs, both ladders, all `(i,j)`: 540/540. Equivalently `R^{AB}_{s,i,j}·Δ = 0`: 540/540.\n- **3×3 matrix (cell 12).** No row vanishes identically on the diagonal. 732 of 816 triples of rows give `det N^{AA} ≠ 0` for all 6 states; the other 84 give zero for all 6 (none partial). At rows `(s,i,j) = (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,1)`: norms 6/6 nonzero, cross determinants 30/30 zero, `N^{AB}·Δ = 0` for 30/30, and no cross pair with `N^{AB} ≡ 0` — including the two same-weight octets.\n\n**Open / next.** (i) Which rows are natural (the 84 degenerate triples should have a structural reason, cf. the `i ≥ j` rule at gl(4)). (ii) Relation of `det N^{AA}` to the Hilbert-space norm `⟨Ψ_A|Ψ_A⟩` of the explicit eigenvectors in `states`. (iii) Twisted version, where the Cartan charges re-enter and the descendants separate.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. The explicit matrix at the simplest working rows\n\nThe first working triple is `(s,i,j) = (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,1)`: all three rows on the **ladder of site 1**, pairing the direct `q_1, q_2` of `B` with the duals `q^1, q^2` of `A`.\n\n**Bracket.** For a polynomial `f`,\n\n$$\\langle f \\rangle \\;\\equiv\\; \\oint_{C_1}\\frac{du}{2\\pi i}\\;\\frac{\\mu(u)}{\\nu_1(u)\\,\\nu_1(u-h)}\\,f(u)\\;=\\;\\oint_{C_1}\\frac{du}{2\\pi i}\\;\\frac{f(u)}{\\prod_{\\alpha=1}^{2}(u-\\theta_\\alpha)(u-\\theta_\\alpha-h)(u-\\theta_\\alpha-2h)(u-\\theta_\\alpha-3h)},$$\n\nwhere `C_1` encircles only `u = θ_1, θ_1+h, θ_1+2h, θ_1+3h`. Here `μ = ∏_α 1/((u-θ_α)(u-θ_α-h)) ∝ Γ[ν_1^{[2]}]/Γ[ν_3^{[2]}]` and `ν_1(u) = (u-θ_1-2h)(u-θ_2-2h)`.\n\n**Matrix.** With `q_i^{[-2]}(u) = q_i(u-h)`, `q_i` the direct solutions (`O q_i^{[2]} = 0`, increasing degree) and `q^j` the duals (`O^† q^j = 0`, `deg q^j = μ_j + 3 - j`):\n\n$$N^{AB} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n\\big\\langle q^1_A\\,\\big(u^2\\, q^{B[-2]}_1 - \\nu_1^{[-2]}\\, q^B_1\\big)\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^1_A\\; u\\; q^{B[-2]}_1\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^1_A\\; q^{B[-2]}_1\\big\\rangle \\\\[4pt]\n\\big\\langle q^2_A\\,\\big(u^2\\, q^{B[-2]}_1 - \\nu_1^{[-2]}\\, q^B_1\\big)\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^2_A\\; u\\; q^{B[-2]}_1\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^2_A\\; q^{B[-2]}_1\\big\\rangle \\\\[4pt]\n\\big\\langle q^1_A\\,\\big(u^2\\, q^{B[-2]}_2 - \\nu_1^{[-2]}\\, q^B_2\\big)\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^1_A\\; u\\; q^{B[-2]}_2\\big\\rangle & \\big\\langle q^1_A\\; q^{B[-2]}_2\\big\\rangle\n\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\nN^{AB}\\begin{pmatrix}\\Delta t_1\\\\ \\Delta t_{21}\\\\ \\Delta t_{20}\\end{pmatrix} = 0,$$\n\nwith `T^A_1 - T^B_1 = Δt_1` and `T^A_2 - T^B_2 = Δt_1 u^2 + Δt_{21} u + Δt_{20}`. Row `r` is the orthogonality identity `⟨q^j_A[-ΔT_1 ν_1^{[-2]} q^B_i + ΔT_2 q^{B[-2]}_i]⟩ = 0` for its `(i,j)`, split by the coefficients of `ΔT_1, ΔT_2`. So `det N^{AB} = 0` for `A ≠ B`, and `det N^{AA}` is the norm.\n\nThe cell below evaluates it at `θ_1 = 1/3, θ_2 = -8/57, h = 1` for the two octets `8_1, 8_2` (same weight `{3,2,1}`, same `T_1`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 6. Explicit N^{AB} at rows (s,i,j) = (1,1,1),(1,1,2),(1,2,1), for the two octets. ---- *)\nClearAll[bracket, NexplicitSym, rowsSimple, oct1, oct2];\nrowsSimple = {{1, 1, 1}, {1, 1, 2}, {1, 2, 1}};\n(* independent re-implementation of the bracket straight from the displayed formula, to cross-check rowR *)\nbracket[f_, x_] := Total[Residue[(f/Product[(x - th) (x - th - h) (x - th - 2 h) (x - th - 3 h), {th, {θ1, θ2}}]) /. prm, {x, #}] & /@ ((θ1 + Range[0, 3] h) /. prm)];\nNexplicit[A_, B_] := Module[{x, hh = h /. prm}, Table[With[{i = ij[[1]], j = ij[[2]]},\n    {bracket[qA[A, j][x] (x^2 qB[B, i][x - hh] - (ν1[x - h] /. prm) qB[B, i][x]), x], bracket[qA[A, j][x] x qB[B, i][x - hh], x], bracket[qA[A, j][x] qB[B, i][x - hh], x]}], {ij, {{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 1}}}]];\noct1 = SelectFirst[states, #[\"mu\"] == {3, 2, 1} && #[\"copy\"] == 1 &];\noct2 = SelectFirst[states, #[\"mu\"] == {3, 2, 1} && #[\"copy\"] == 2 &];\nsameAsRowR = And @@ Flatten@Table[Together[Nexplicit[A, B] - (rowR[A, B, Sequence @@ #] & /@ rowsSimple)] === ConstantArray[0, {3, 3}], {A, states}, {B, states}];\nWith[{N11 = Nexplicit[oct1, oct1], N12 = Nexplicit[oct1, oct2], N21 = Nexplicit[oct2, oct1], d12 = dInv[oct1, oct2]},\n Grid[{\n   {\"bracket formula = rowR at these rows, all 36 ordered pairs\", sameAsRowR},\n   {\"q_1, q_2 of 8_1\", Column[qpoly[#, u] & /@ oct1[\"q\"][[1 ;; 2]]]}, {\"q^1, q^2 of 8_1\", Column[{qpoly[oct1[\"qd\"][[3]], u], qpoly[oct1[\"qd\"][[2]], u]}]},\n   {\"q_1, q_2 of 8_2\", Column[qpoly[#, u] & /@ oct2[\"q\"][[1 ;; 2]]]}, {\"q^1, q^2 of 8_2\", Column[{qpoly[oct2[\"qd\"][[3]], u], qpoly[oct2[\"qd\"][[2]], u]}]},\n   {\"N^{AA}, A = 8_1\", MatrixForm[N11]}, {\"det N^{AA}\", Det[N11]},\n   {\"N^{AB}, A = 8_1, B = 8_2\", MatrixForm[N12]}, {\"det N^{AB}\", Det[N12]},\n   {\"(Δt1, Δt21, Δt20) = T(8_1) - T(8_2)\", d12}, {\"N^{AB}.Δ\", N12 . d12},\n   {\"N^{BA}, A = 8_2, B = 8_1\", MatrixForm[N21]}, {\"det N^{BA}\", Det[N21]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
